se,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":63,"content":"Serve SPA from GET / on any node. Sign-up form with visible error on invalid input; auto-login on success. Logout/login restores same workspace. Store bearer in localStorage huddle.token (or accepted fallbacks). Three-pane layout shell: coloured sidebar + message pane + on-demand thread panel. Workspace identity in sidebar. Stable selectors: auth-form, auth-submit, auth-toggle, auth-modal, workspace-create-form, empty-state-create-workspace, join-workspace-*, current-user, logout-btn, workspace-header, channel-list, dms-list. Drivable at 1280x900.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":66,"content":"# MARATHON-16 — SPA: auth, token storage, workspace shell","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":70,"content":"Replace the stub `GET /` HTML with a zero-build Huddle SPA served identically from every HTTP node. The SPA owns browser session lifecycle (register → auto-login, login, logout), durable bearer storage under `localStorage` key `huddle.token` (with documented read fallbacks), restoration of the last workspace after logout/login, and the three-pane workspace shell (coloured sidebar + main message pane + on-demand thread panel) with the epic’s stable `data-testid` selectors so CUA/Playwright can drive auth and workspace onboarding at 1280×900. Messaging, channel CRUD UI, and settings modals remain later SPA tasks; this task only mounts their shell slots and wires the seams that already exist (Auth + Workspaces APIs).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":82,"content":"| Token storage | Write **`localStorage[\"huddle.token\"]`**; read primary then accepted fallbacks (below) |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":85,"content":"| Selectors | Stable **`data-testid=\"<name>\"`** attributes matching the task list exactly |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":94,"content":"- Writing only `huddle.token` while accepting read fallbacks matches the task wording and MARATHON-3’s named key without breaking graders that seed alternate keys.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":101,"content":"| Cookie/session auth | Contradicts bearer + `huddle.token` contract already locked by MARATHON-3 |","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":114,"content":"From **MARATHON-3**: `UserObj` key set; `{error:{code,message}}`; register/login `{user,token}`; `/api/auth/me`; bearer parsing; username/password validation rules; store token as `huddle.token`.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":120,"content":"Design complete for SPA auth/token/shell. Zero-build static SPA at GET /; huddle.token + fallbacks; three-pane shell + stable data-testids. Join form wired to POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join (server owned by MARATHON-7). Ready for lead review — keep frontend label for implementer after architect approval.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"../ws/sessions/20260822-231530-app-architect-1--75625568/prompt.txt","matches":[{"lineNumber":131,"content":"#### 3i. Acceptance Criteria","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"../ws/sessions/20260822-231142-app-architect-1--6d670797/metadata.json","matches":[{"lineNumber":4,"content":"  \"task_id\": \"MARATHON-16\",","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"../ws/sessions/20260822-231142-app-architect-1--6d670797/prompt.txt","matches":[{"lineNumber":56,"content":"A task is already claimed for you: **MARATHON-16**. Work on that one and no other.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":58,"content":"ID: MARATHON-16","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":67,"content":"Serve SPA from GET / on any node. Sign-up form with visible error on invalid input; auto-login on success. Logout/login restores same workspace. Store bearer in localStorage huddle.token (or accepted fallbacks). Three-pane layout shell: coloured sidebar + message pane + on-demand thread panel. Workspace identity in sidebar. Stable selectors: auth-form, auth-submit, auth-toggle, auth-modal, workspace-create-form, empty-state-create-workspace, join-workspace-*, current-user, logout-btn, workspace-header, channel-list, dms-list. Drivable at 1280x900.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":131,"content":"#### 3i. Acceptance Criteria","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"../ws/sessions/20260822-230008-backend-dev-1--cfebd2ac/prompt.txt","matches":[{"lineNumber":71,"content":"This task adds the workspace tenancy root for Huddle: authenticated callers can create a workspace (unique kebab `slug`, display `name`, creator as `owner`, default `join_mode=open`), which atomically provisions the public `#general` channel and membership rows; list workspaces they own or belong to; and load a workspace by slug with the visible channel list plus embedded `read_state`. It locks `WorkspaceObj`, the initial `ChannelObj` shape used by later channel APIs, the SQLite schema for workspaces/members/channels, and the REST contracts the SPA shell (MARATHON-16) and members/channels tasks (MARATHON-6/7) consume.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"../ws/sessions/20260822-225557-qa-engineer-1--a31b83ee/prompt.txt","matches":[{"lineNumber":78,"content":"#### 2b. Turn the Acceptance Criteria Into a Checklist","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"../ws/sessions/20260822-225358-app-architect-1--52da21f4/prompt.txt","matches":[{"lineNumber":74,"content":"This task adds the workspace tenancy root for Huddle: authenticated callers can create a workspace (unique kebab `slug`, display `name`, creator as `owner`, default `join_mode=open`), which atomically provisions the public `#general` channel and membership rows; list workspaces they own or belong to; and load a workspace by slug with the visible channel list plus embedded `read_state`. It locks `WorkspaceObj`, the initial `ChannelObj` shape used by later channel APIs, the SQLite schema for workspaces/members/channels, and the REST contracts the SPA shell (MARATHON-16) and members/channels tasks (MARATHON-6/7) consume.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":186,"content":"#### 3i. Acceptance Criteria","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"../ws/sessions/20260822-225357-qa-engineer-1--9f00e719/prompt.txt","matches":[{"lineNumber":83,"content":"#### 2b. Turn the Acceptance Criteria Into a Checklist","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"../ws/sessions/20260822-224803-app-architect-1--075fc85a/prompt.txt","matches":[{"lineNumber":131,"content":"#### 3i. Acceptance Criteria","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"../ws/sessions/20260822-224450-app-architect-1--d78bac5a/prompt.txt","matches":[{"lineNumber":131,"content":"#### 3i. Acceptance Criteria","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"../ws/sessions/20260822-223939-qa-engineer-1--e0547f00/prompt.txt","matches":[{"lineNumber":82,"content":"#### 2b. Turn the Acceptance Criteria Into a Checklist","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"../ws/sessions/20260822-223733-backend-dev-1--b08fae58/prompt.txt","matches":[{"lineNumber":91,"content":"- Opaque bearer tokens match the epic (“REST + bearer auth”) and the SPA task (`localStorage` `huddle.token`) without JWT clock skew or shared signing secrets across processes.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"../ws/sessions/20260822-223723-qa-engineer-1--84602393/prompt.txt","matches":[{"lineNumber":83,"content":"#### 2b. Turn the Acceptance Criteria Into a Checklist","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"../ws/sessions/20260822-223053-app-architect-1--c6426f65/prompt.txt","matches":[{"lineNumber":131,"content":"#### 3i. Acceptance Criteria","contentTruncated":fals