{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-d83bbc07-f6f7-43b9-adf8-7608497fa38c-32\nfc_3048e1fe-21f7-9d73-9090-c31625e8dbcb_0","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"which loom; loom data show MARATHON-16 --output json 2>&1 | head -c 80000","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-d83bbc07-f6f7-43b9-adf8-7608497fa38c-32\nfc_3048e1fe-21f7-9d73-9090-c31625e8dbcb_0","simpleCommands":["which","loom","head"],"hasInputRedirect":false,"hasOutputRedirect":true,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"which","args":[{"type":"word","value":"loom"}],"fullText":"which loom"},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"show"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON-16"},{"type":"word","value":"--output"},{"type":"word","value":"json"}],"fullText":"loom data show MARATHON-16 --output json"},{"name":"head","args":[{"type":"word","value":"-c"},{"type":"number","value":"80000"}],"fullText":"head -c 80000"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":true,"redirects":[{"operator":">&","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"number","targetText":"1"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Fetch MARATHON-16 task with design","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"8c9f2801-d9d1-4b4e-ac13-8ec9ab25b62b","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"result":{"success":{"command":"which loom; loom data show MARATHON-16 --output json 2>&1 | head -c 80000","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"/installed-agent/loom-marathon/bin/loom\ntime=2026-08-22T23:36:14.602Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\n{\n  \"id\": \"MARATHON-16\",\n  \"title\": \"SPA: auth, token storage, workspace shell\",\n  \"status\": \"review\",\n  \"priority\": 1,\n  \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n  \"owner\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"labels\": [\n    \"frontend\"\n  ],\n  \"source_repo\": \"app\",\n  \"parent\": \"MARATHON-1\",\n  \"design\": \"# MARATHON-16 — SPA: auth, token storage, workspace shell\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nReplace the stub `GET /` HTML with a zero-build Huddle SPA served identically from every HTTP node. The SPA owns browser session lifecycle (register → auto-login, login, logout), durable bearer storage under `localStorage` key `huddle.token` (with documented read fallbacks), restoration of the last workspace after logout/login, and the three-pane workspace shell (coloured sidebar + main message pane + on-demand thread panel) with the epic’s stable `data-testid` selectors so CUA/Playwright can drive auth and workspace onboarding at 1280×900. Messaging, channel CRUD UI, and settings modals remain later SPA tasks; this task only mounts their shell slots and wires the seams that already exist (Auth + Workspaces APIs).\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n\\n### Decision\\n\\n| Concern | Choice |\\n|--------|--------|\\n| Delivery | **Static SPA** under `/app/static/` served by FastAPI; `GET /` returns `static/index.html` on every node |\\n| Frontend stack | **Vanilla HTML + CSS + ES modules** — no Node, no bundler, no React |\\n| API access | Same-origin relative `/api/...` (works on `:8000`/`:8001`/`:8002` without CORS or hard-coded ports) |\\n| Auth header | `Authorization: Bearer \\u003ctoken\\u003e` exactly as MARATHON-3 |\\n| Token storage | Write **`localStorage[\\\"huddle.token\\\"]`**; read primary then accepted fallbacks (below) |\\n| Workspace restore | Persist **`localStorage[\\\"huddle.workspaceSlug\\\"]`** across logout; re-select after next login |\\n| Routing | **Hash routes** (`#/`, `#/w/{slug}`) — no server path rewrite; refresh-safe on any node |\\n| Selectors | Stable **`data-testid=\\\"\\u003cname\\u003e\\\"`** attributes matching the task list exactly |\\n| Shell layout | Fixed three-pane: sidebar (coloured) \\\\| message pane \\\\| thread panel (hidden until opened) |\\n\\n### Why\\n\\n- Epic requires browser UI at `GET /` with stable selectors; MARATHON-2 explicitly deferred SPA to this task and left a stub.\\n- Zero-build static assets keep `start.sh` / Python-only ops unchanged (no second runtime), matching MARATHON-2’s self-contained cluster.\\n- Same-origin `/api` + shared SQLite tokens already work cross-node (MARATHON-3/22); the SPA must not invent per-node cookies or JWT.\\n- Hash routing avoids FastAPI catch-all complexity and keeps `GET /api/*` unambiguous.\\n- Writing only `huddle.token` while accepting read fallbacks matches the task wording and MARATHON-3’s named key without breaking graders that seed alternate keys.\\n\\n### Alternatives considered\\n\\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\\n|------------|------------------|\\n| React/Vite SPA with build step | Requires Node in `start.sh` / image; epic forbids remote services and prefers self-contained boot |\\n| Cookie/session auth | Contradicts bearer + `huddle.token` contract already locked by MARATHON-3 |\\n| Path-based SPA routes (`/w/acme`) without catch-all | Refresh on deep links 404 unless every node mounts a rewrite; hash is simpler |\\n| Server-rendered auth forms | Breaks SPA continuity for MARATHON-17/18 and CUA driving a single document |\\n| Invent join/members REST in this task | Owned by MARATHON-6/7/12; SPA locks client seam only |\\n\\n### Trade-off accepted\\n\\nJoin-workspace UI is **mounted and wired** to a join REST seam that MARATHON-7 (open-workspace auto-onboard / join) must implement. Until that endpoint exists, submit shows the server error envelope (or a clear network failure). Create-workspace is the fully working onboarding path today. We accept temporary join failures over inventing a second membership SoT in the SPA task.\\n\\n### Conventions inherited (must not diverge)\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-2**: Product **Huddle**; `GET /` is HTML 200 on every node; `/api/...` JSON; no DinD.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-3**: `UserObj` key set; `{error:{code,message}}`; register/login `{user,token}`; `/api/auth/me`; bearer parsing; username/password validation rules; store token as `huddle.token`.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-4**: Same `UserObj`; profile PATCH not required in this shell (settings UI is MARATHON-18).\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-5**: `WorkspaceObj` / `ChannelObj` / full `ReadStateEntry`; `POST/GET /api/workspaces`, `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}`; create body `{slug,name}`; non-member detail → 404.\\n\\n## Interface Contracts\\n\\n### Selector contract (SPA ↔ grader / CUA)\\n\\nAll names below are **`data-testid` values**. They must be present in the DOM when the corresponding UI state is visible (not merely in JS strings). Prefer exactly these strings — no prefixes.\\n\\n| `data-testid` | When visible | Role |\\n|---------------|--------------|------|\\n| `auth-modal` | Unauthenticated (or forced re-auth) | Modal/dialog wrapping the auth form |\\n| `auth-form` | Inside auth modal | `\\u003cform\\u003e` for register or login |\\n| `auth-submit` | Inside auth form | Submit control |\\n| `auth-toggle` | Inside auth modal | Control that switches register ↔ login mode |\\n| `auth-error` | After failed auth attempt | Visible text node showing `error.message` (or client validation message). **Must not** be empty/invisible on 400/401/409. |\\n| `workspace-create-form` | Authenticated empty / onboarding | Form to create workspace (`slug` + `name`) |\\n| `empty-state-create-workspace` | Authenticated with **zero** workspaces | Empty-state control/region that focuses or reveals create form |\\n| `join-workspace-form` | Authenticated empty / onboarding | Form to join by workspace slug |\\n| `join-workspace-slug` | Inside join form | Text input for slug |\\n| `join-workspace-submit` | Inside join form | Submit control |\\n| `join-workspace-error` | After failed join | Visible error text |\\n| `current-user` | Authenticated shell | Shows session user’s `display_name` (fallback `username`) |\\n| `logout-btn` | Authenticated shell | Clears token and returns to auth modal |\\n| `workspace-header` | Authenticated **with** current workspace | Shows workspace identity (`name` and/or `slug`) |\\n| `channel-list` | Authenticated with current workspace | Container for non-DM channels (may be empty of children until channels load / MARATHON-17) |\\n| `dms-list` | Authenticated with current workspace | Container for DM channels (empty until MARATHON-9/17) |\\n\\n**Auth form fields (required for drivability, not all named in the task list):**\\n\\n| `data-testid` | Element |\\n|---------------|---------|\\n| `auth-username` | Username input |\\n| `auth-password` | Password input |\\n| `auth-display-name` | Optional display name; **visible in register mode only** |\\n\\n**Workspace create fields:**\\n\\n| `data-testid` | Element |\\n|---------------|---------|\\n| `workspace-slug` | Slug input |\\n| `workspace-name` | Name input |\\n| `workspace-create-submit` | Submit |\\n| `workspace-create-error` | Visible error |\\n\\n**Shell slots for dependents (mount now, behavior later):**\\n\\n| `data-testid` | Behavior in this task |\\n|---------------|----------------------|\\n| `message-pane` | Always present when shell is shown; may show placeholder copy (“Select a channel” / empty). **No** message composer required here. |\\n| `thread-panel` | Present in DOM; **`hidden` / not displayed** by default (`display:none` or equivalent). MARATHON-17 opens it. |\\n\\n### Token storage contract (browser ↔ SPA)\\n\\n| Operation | Behavior |\\n|-----------|----------|\\n| **Write (register/login success)** | `localStorage.setItem(\\\"huddle.token\\\", token)` where `token` is the opaque string from the API. Also remove stale fallback keys if present (optional hygiene). |\\n| **Read (boot / API client)** | First non-empty string among, in order: `huddle.token`, `huddle_token`, `token`. Treat whitespace-only as missing. |\\n| **Clear (logout or 401 from `/me`)** | Remove **all** of: `huddle.token`, `huddle_token`, `token`. |\\n| **Workspace slug persist** | On successful workspace select/create/restore: `localStorage.setItem(\\\"huddle.workspaceSlug\\\", slug)`. **Do not** clear this on logout (required for “logout/login restores same workspace”). |\\n| **Negative** | Must **not** store the bearer in cookies, `sessionStorage` only, or URL query strings. |\\n\\n### Seam: Browser ↔ `GET /` (and static assets)\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Server (each node)** | `GET /` → **200** `text/html` document that boots the SPA (title/brand includes **Huddle**). Serve `/static/*` assets with correct MIME types. No auth required. |\\n| **Client** | Load JS; run boot sequence below. |\\n\\n**Failure / slow:** TCP errors until node respawn (≤60s) — same as MARATHON-2. Asset 404 → blank UI; implementer must keep relative paths correct.\\n\\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/auth/register`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client** | Body `{username, password, display_name?}` matching MARATHON-3. Disable `auth-submit` while in flight. On **201**: store token, set session user from `user`, close/hide auth modal, continue boot (list workspaces). On **400/409**: show `error.message` in `auth-error` (visible). On network/5xx: show a generic visible error in `auth-error`. |\\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-3). |\\n\\n**Auto-login:** Register success **is** login — do **not** require a second login call. Token from register response is sufficient.\\n\\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/auth/login`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client** | Body `{username, password}`. Same storage + navigation as register. On **401/400**: visible `auth-error` with `error.message`. |\\n| **Server** | Unchanged. |\\n\\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `GET /api/auth/me`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client** | On boot if a token is readable: call with bearer. While pending: show a lightweight boot placeholder; **do not** flash the auth modal if a token exists. On **200**: set session user from `user`. On **401**: clear all token keys; show auth modal. |\\n| **Server** | Unchanged. |\\n\\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `GET /api/workspaces` / `POST /api/workspaces` / `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client** | All calls send bearer. **List** after auth: if `workspaces.length === 0`, show empty state (`empty-state-create-workspace` + create + join forms). If non-empty: prefer `huddle.workspaceSlug` if it appears in the list; else first list item (sorted as server returns). **Create**: `POST` `{slug,name}`; on **201** persist slug, load detail, enter shell. On **400/409** show `workspace-create-error`. **Detail**: populate `workspace-header`, split `channels` into `channel-list` (`is_dm === false`) and `dms-list` (`is_dm === true`); ignore `read_state` badges in this task (optional no-op). On detail **404**: clear invalid stored slug, fall back to list/empty. On any **401**: logout locally. |\\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-5). |\\n\\n**Channel row markup (minimal, for MARATHON-17):** each channel entry **should** expose `data-channel-id=\\\"{id}\\\"` and `data-channel-name=\\\"{name}\\\"` when listed. Display name may show `#` prefix for non-DM; stored `name` remains without `#`.\\n\\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join` (client locked here; server owned by MARATHON-7)\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client** | Body `{}` (ignore extras). Bearer required. Disable submit while in flight. On **200** with `{workspace: WorkspaceObj}` (optional `channels` / `read_state` if server returns them): persist slug, enter shell (fetch detail if channels omitted). On **4xx**: show `error.message` in `join-workspace-error`. |\\n| **Server (MARATHON-7)** | For `join_mode=open`, add caller as `member` if not already; return 200. For `invite_only`, **403** (invitations are MARATHON-12). Unknown slug → **404** envelope. Idempotent if already a member → **200**. |\\n\\n**Until MARATHON-7 lands:** SPA still renders join controls; failed submit must surface a visible error (not a silent no-op).\\n\\n### HTTP client rules (SPA owns)\\n\\n1. `Content-Type: application/json` on POST bodies.\\n2. Parse JSON error envelope; never assume FastAPI `detail`.\\n3. Timeouts: recommend ~15s; on abort/network error show visible error on the active form.\\n4. Do not retry 401/409 blindly; do not infinite-retry `/me`.\\n\\n### Auth modal UX\\n\\n- Default mode on first visit: **register** (sign-up), matching “Sign-up form with visible error…”.\\n- `auth-toggle` switches to login and back; update submit label/copy accordingly.\\n- Client-side pre-check may mirror username/password rules for faster UX, but **server messages win** on response.\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n### Browser (no SQLite changes in this task)\\n\\n| Key | Type | Lifetime | Notes |\\n|-----|------|----------|-------|\\n| `localStorage[\\\"huddle.token\\\"]` | string | Until logout / 401 | Canonical bearer |\\n| `localStorage[\\\"huddle_token\\\"]` | string | Read fallback only | Accepted fallback |\\n| `localStorage[\\\"token\\\"]` | string | Read fallback only | Accepted fallback |\\n| `localStorage[\\\"huddle.workspaceSlug\\\"]` | string | Survives logout | Last workspace slug |\\n\\n### In-memory SPA state (not persisted)\\n\\n| Field | Type | Notes |\\n|-------|------|-------|\\n| `user` | `UserObj` \\\\| null | From register/login/`/me` |\\n| `workspaces` | `WorkspaceObj[]` | From list |\\n| `currentWorkspace` | `WorkspaceObj` \\\\| null | Selected |\\n| `channels` | `ChannelObj[]` | From detail |\\n| `authMode` | `\\\"register\\\"` \\\\| `\\\"login\\\"` | Modal mode |\\n| `threadOpen` | boolean | Default `false` |\\n\\n### Server schema\\n\\n**No migration.** This task does not alter SQLite. Backward compatible with migrations v0–v2.\\n\\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\\n\\n### Create\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `static/index.html` | SPA shell markup: auth modal, empty/onboarding, three-pane layout; all required `data-testid`s; `\\u003ctitle\\u003eHuddle\\u003c/title\\u003e`; script `type=\\\"module\\\"` entry. |\\n| `static/css/app.css` | Layout for 1280×900: coloured sidebar (≥~220px), message pane flex-grow, thread panel (~320px) hidden by default; auth modal overlay; visible error styles (not `visibility:hidden` when populated). |\\n| `static/js/storage.js` | Token read/write/clear with fallbacks; workspace slug get/set. |\\n| `static/js/api.js` | `api(method, path, {token, body})` → JSON; maps envelope errors. |\\n| `static/js/auth_ui.js` | Register/login toggle, submit handlers, auto-login on register, error rendering. |\\n| `static/js/shell.js` | Empty state, create/join forms, workspace header, channel/dms lists, logout, hash routing. |\\n| `static/js/app.js` | Boot: read token → `/me` → list → restore slug → render. |\\n\\n(Implementer may collapse JS files if behavior and selectors match; names above are the preferred split.)\\n\\n### Modify\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `server/app.py` | Replace inline stub HTML with `FileResponse` to `static/index.html` (path resolved from app root). Mount `StaticFiles` at `/static` pointing at `static/`. Keep `/api/health` and routers unchanged. Ensure `/` is registered **before** any catch-all; do not shadow `/api/*`. |\\n| `tests/test_health.py` | Keep asserting `GET /` 200 HTML + `\\\"Huddle\\\"` in body (still true). Optionally assert a stable selector string appears in HTML (e.g. `data-testid=\\\"auth-form\\\"`) — recommended, not mandatory if covered by a new SPA test file. |\\n| `tests/test_spa_shell.py` (create) | TestClient: `/` contains required testids; `/static/...` 200; optional auth flow via API + HTML presence (no browser required for unit). |\\n\\n### Do not modify\\n\\n| File | Reason |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `server/auth/*`, `server/workspaces/*`, `server/users/*` | Contracts already shipped; SPA is consumer only |\\n| `start.sh` | No build step to add |\\n| `timer.sh` | Harness-owned |\\n\\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\\n\\n### Build order within this task\\n\\n1. Static files + `app.py` serve path (unblocks `GET /` HTML checks).\\n2. `storage.js` + `api.js`.\\n3. Auth modal + register/login/`/me` boot.\\n4. Workspace list/create/empty state + slug restore.\\n5. Shell chrome (sidebar colour, header, channel/dms lists, logout, thread slot).\\n6. Join form wired to join seam (tolerate backend absence via visible error).\\n\\n### Parallelism\\n\\n- Can implement entirely in parallel with MARATHON-6/8/9/10/… **except** join success depends on MARATHON-7’s open-workspace join/auto-onboard.\\n- MARATHON-17/18 **must** land after this shell (they depend on this task).\\n\\n### Seams this task owns for dependents\\n\\n| Contract | Consumer |\\n|----------|----------|\\n| `data-testid` shell + auth set above | QA / CUA; MARATHON-17/18 |\\n| `huddle.token` + fallbacks + `huddle.workspaceSlug` | All later SPA tasks |\\n| Hash route `#/w/{slug}` + in-memory workspace/channel selection hooks | MARATHON-17 |\\n| Hidden `thread-panel` slot | MARATHON-17 |\\n| `channel-list` / `dms-list` containers + `data-channel-id` | MARATHON-17 |\\n| Client call shape `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join` | MARATHON-7 must implement server |\\n\\n### Split follow-ups (already exist — do not recreate)\\n\\n- **MARATHON-17** — messages, threads, reactions, channel create/switch UI inside this shell.\\n- **MARATHON-18** — workspace/channel settings modals.\\n- **MARATHON-7** — server join / open auto-onboard so join form succeeds.\\n\\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\\n\\n| Item | Where found | Why excluded |\\n|------|-------------|--------------|\\n| Message composer, edit/delete, reactions, emoji picker | MARATHON-17 description; no message routes yet (MARATHON-8 open) | Dependent SPA task |\\n| Opening/populating `thread-panel` with replies | MARATHON-17 | Shell only mounts hidden slot |\\n| Workspace settings / invitations UI (`workspace-settings-modal`, invitation testids) | MARATHON-18; APIs MARATHON-6/12 | Different task |\\n| Channel create/join/leave/archive/pins REST | `server/channels/store.py` helpers only; no routes | MARATHON-7 |\\n| DM get-or-create | No DM API | MARATHON-9; `dms-list` stays empty-capable |\\n| Profile PATCH UI | `PATCH /api/users/me` exists | MARATHON-18 / settings |\\n| WebSocket subscribe/resume | No WS routes | MARATHON-13 |\\n| Logout token revoke API | MARATHON-3 explicitly out of scope | Client clears storage only |\\n| IRC / Redis fan-out UI | Cluster tasks | Unrelated |\\n| Stub text “Cluster node stub.” | `server/app.py` | Replaced by SPA in this task (in scope to remove) |\\n\\nNeighborhood scan accounted for: `HTMLResponse` stub in `server/app.py`; `tests/test_health.py` + `tests/test_cluster_boot.py` `GET /` HTML assertions (remain valid if brand “Huddle” + HTML document preserved); no existing `static/` tree; no `localStorage` / `data-testid` hits in-repo yet.\\n\\n## Edge Cases \\u0026 Error Handling\\n\\n| Case | Expected behavior |\\n|------|-------------------|\\n| Invalid register username/password (client or 400) | Show message in **visible** `auth-error`; stay on form; do **not** store token |\\n| Register username taken (409) | Visible `auth-error` with server message; no token write |\\n| Login bad credentials (401) | Visible `auth-error`; no token write |\\n| Register success | Store token; treat as logged in; **no** manual login step |\\n| Boot with valid token | `/me` then workspace flow; auth modal **not** shown |\\n| Boot with garbage token | `/me` 401 → clear tokens → auth modal |\\n| Boot with fallback key only (`token` set, `huddle.token` absent) | Read fallback; on next successful login/register rewrite canonical `huddle.token` |\\n| Logout | Clear token keys; show auth modal; **keep** `huddle.workspaceSlug`; clear in-memory user/channels |\\n| Login after logout with same user | Restore workspace from `huddle.workspaceSlug` if still a member; else first workspace or empty state |\\n| Stored slug for workspace user left / never joined | Detail 404 → drop slug selection; re-list; do not loop |\\n| Create workspace validation/conflict | Visible `workspace-create-error`; remain on form |\\n| Join before MARATHON-7 (404/405/network) | Visible `join-workspace-error`; do not fake membership client-side |\\n| API slow | Disable active submit; keep prior UI; no double-submit |\\n| `GET /` on :8001/:8002 | Same SPA bytes/behavior as :8000 |\\n| Thread panel default | Not visible; must **not** cover message pane at 1280×900 |\\n| Empty channel/dms lists | Containers still present with testids; empty children OK |\\n| Password in DOM errors | Never echo password into `auth-error` |\\n| Unknown JSON fields from server | Ignore extras; do not crash |\\n| `include_archived` | Shell detail calls **omit** query (default hide archived) |\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `GET http://127.0.0.1:800{0,1,2}/` → **200** HTML containing brand **Huddle** and bootstraps the SPA (script/CSS load without 404).\\n2. Unauthenticated visit shows `auth-modal`, `auth-form`, `auth-submit`, `auth-toggle`.\\n3. Sign-up with invalid input (e.g. short password) shows a **visible** error (readable in `auth-error` / form error UI); must **not** set `huddle.token`.\\n4. Sign-up with valid input → **201** path: token stored at `localStorage[\\\"huddle.token\\\"]` (len ≥ 16); user is logged in **without** a separate login submit; auth modal dismissed.\\n5. `auth-toggle` switches to login; successful login also stores `huddle.token` and enters authenticated UI.\\n6. Authenticated zero-workspace state exposes `empty-state-create-workspace`, `workspace-create-form`, and `join-workspace-form` / `join-workspace-slug` / `join-workspace-submit`.\\n7. Creating a workspace via the form calls `POST /api/workspaces` and then shows shell with `workspace-header`, `channel-list`, `dms-list`, `current-user`, `logout-btn`, `message-pane`, and hidden `thread-panel`.\\n8. Sidebar is visually distinct (coloured) from the message pane; workspace identity appears in the sidebar/`workspace-header`.\\n9. Logout via `logout-btn` clears bearer storage (all token keys) and returns to auth UI; `huddle.workspaceSlug` remains.\\n10. Logging in again as the same user restores the previous workspace (same slug in header/lists) without manually re-picking, when membership still exists.\\n11. Layout is usable at **1280×900** without requiring horizontal scrolling for the three-pane shell (thread collapsed).\\n12. Negative: authenticated API calls must **not** omit the `Authorization` header when a token is present.\\n13. Negative: must **not** leave the MARATHON-2 stub-only body (“Cluster node stub”) as the sole `GET /` content.\\n14. Negative: must **not** require Node/npm to build assets for `start.sh` boot.\\n15. Reading a bearer from fallback key `token` or `huddle_token` still authenticates on boot if `/me` succeeds.\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Automated\\n\\n- Extend/keep `tests/test_health.py` + cluster boot: `GET /` HTML 200 + Huddle.\\n- Add `tests/test_spa_shell.py` (TestClient): document contains critical `data-testid`s; `/static/js/app.js` (or chosen entry) returns 200; optional flow register via API then assert token key documented (storage is browser-only — HTML/API integration is enough at unit layer).\\n\\n### Manual / CUA (primary)\\n\\n1. `./start.sh`; open `http://127.0.0.1:8000/` at 1280×900.\\n2. Register invalid user → see error; register valid → land in empty/create state; confirm DevTools `localStorage[\\\"huddle.token\\\"]`.\\n3. Create workspace → sidebar shows name/slug; `#general` appears under `channel-list`.\\n4. Logout → login → same workspace restored.\\n5. Repeat load on `:8001` with same token (paste or shared storage isn’t cross-port — instead register on 8000, copy token into 8001 `localStorage`, reload) → `/me` works (cluster SoT).\\n6. Confirm thread panel not visible; message pane placeholder visible.\\n7. Toggle auth register/login; confirm selectors exist for Playwright (`document.querySelector('[data-testid=\\\"auth-form\\\"]')` etc.).\\n\\n### Out of test scope here\\n\\nFull message/thread/reaction flows (MARATHON-17); settings/invitations (MARATHON-18); successful open-workspace join (blocked on MARATHON-7 server).\",\n  \"design_format\": \"markdown\",\n  \"has_design\": true,\n  \"notes\": \"IMPL: Zero-build SPA at GET / (static/). Token write huddle.token; read fallbacks huddle_token/token. Workspace restore via huddle.workspaceSlug across logout. Join form POSTs /api/workspaces/{slug}/join (server still MARATHON-7). Verified via pytest + Playwright at 1280x900 (register/login/create/logout/restore; thread panel hidden).\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:47.179119571Z\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-22T23:35:12.247305911Z\",\n  \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"description\": \"Serve SPA from GET / on any node. Sign-up form with visible error on invalid input; auto-login on success. Logout/login restores same workspace. Store bearer in localStorage huddle.token (or accepted fallbacks). Three-pane layout shell: coloured sidebar + message pane + on-demand thread panel. Workspace identity in sidebar. Stable selectors: auth-form, auth-submit, auth-toggle, auth-modal, workspace-create-form, empty-state-create-workspace, join-workspace-*, current-user, logout-btn, workspace-header, channel-list, dms-list. Drivable at 1280x900.\",\n  \"dependents\": [\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-17\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-16\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"SPA: channels, messages, threads, reactions\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"priority\": 1,\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:56.201269638Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-18\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-16\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"SPA: workspace and channel settings UI\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"priority\": 2,\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:56.275071493Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": 26,\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-16\",\n      \"author\": \"marathon-harness\",\n      \"text\": \"DESIGN-AUTO-APPROVED pass=11\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T23:29:16.865171828Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 27,\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-16\",\n      \"author\": \"frontend-dev-1\",\n      \"text\": \"IMPL-DONE attempt=1 commit=f4cf48192856189c3c1d1231aced023485e76550\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T23:35:12.229157039Z\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","stderr":"","executionTime":129,"interleavedOutput":"/installed-agent/loom-marathon/bin/loom\ntime=2026-08-22T23:36:14.602Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:44829\n{\n  \"id\": \"MARATHON-16\",\n  \"title\": \"SPA: auth, token storage, workspace shell\",\n  \"status\": \"review\",\n  \"priority\": 1,\n  \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n  \"owner\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"labels\": [\n    \"frontend\"\n  ],\n  \"source_repo\": \"app\",\n  \"parent\": \"MARATHON-1\",\n  \"design\": \"# MARATHON-16 — SPA: auth, token storage, workspace shell\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nReplace the stub `GET /` HTML with a zero-build Huddle SPA served identically from every HTTP node. The SPA owns browser session lifecycle (register → auto-login, login, logout), durable bearer storage under `localStorage` key `huddle.token` (with documented read fallbacks), restoration of the last workspace after logout/login, and the three-pane workspace shell (coloured sidebar + main message pane + on-demand thread panel) with the epic’s stable `data-testid` selectors so CUA/Playwright can drive auth and workspace onboarding at 1280×900. Messaging, channel CRUD UI, and settings modals remain later SPA tasks; this task only mounts their shell slots and wires the seams that already exist (Auth + Workspaces APIs).\\n\\n## Technical Approach\\n\\n### Decision\\n\\n| Concern | Choice |\\n|--------|--------|\\n| Delivery | **Static SPA** under `/app/static/` served by FastAPI; `GET /` returns `static/index.html` on every node |\\n| Frontend stack | **Vanilla HTML + CSS + ES modules** — no Node, no bundler, no React |\\n| API access | Same-origin relative `/api/...` (works on `:8000`/`:8001`/`:8002` without CORS or hard-coded ports) |\\n| Auth header | `Authorization: Bearer \\u003ctoken\\u003e` exactly as MARATHON-3 |\\n| Token storage | Write **`localStorage[\\\"huddle.token\\\"]`**; read primary then accepted fallbacks (below) |\\n| Workspace restore | Persist **`localStorage[\\\"huddle.workspaceSlug\\\"]`** across logout; re-select after next login |\\n| Routing | **Hash routes** (`#/`, `#/w/{slug}`) — no server path rewrite; refresh-safe on any node |\\n| Selectors | Stable **`data-testid=\\\"\\u003cname\\u003e\\\"`** attributes matching the task list exactly |\\n| Shell layout | Fixed three-pane: sidebar (coloured) \\\\| message pane \\\\| thread panel (hidden until opened) |\\n\\n### Why\\n\\n- Epic requires browser UI at `GET /` with stable selectors; MARATHON-2 explicitly deferred SPA to this task and left a stub.\\n- Zero-build static assets keep `start.sh` / Python-only ops unchanged (no second runtime), matching MARATHON-2’s self-contained cluster.\\n- Same-origin `/api` + shared SQLite tokens already work cross-node (MARATHON-3/22); the SPA must not invent per-node cookies or JWT.\\n- Hash routing avoids FastAPI catch-all complexity and keeps `GET /api/*` unambiguous.\\n- Writing only `huddle.token` while accepting read fallbacks matches the task wording and MARATHON-3’s named key without breaking graders that seed alternate keys.\\n\\n### Alternatives considered\\n\\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\\n|------------|------------------|\\n| React/Vite SPA with build step | Requires Node in `start.sh` / image; epic forbids remote services and prefers self-contained boot |\\n| Cookie/session auth | Contradicts bearer + `huddle.token` contract already locked by MARATHON-3 |\\n| Path-based SPA routes (`/w/acme`) without catch-all | Refresh on deep links 404 unless every node mounts a rewrite; hash is simpler |\\n| Server-rendered auth forms | Breaks SPA continuity for MARATHON-17/18 and CUA driving a single document |\\n| Invent join/members REST in this task | Owned by MARATHON-6/7/12; SPA locks client seam only |\\n\\n### Trade-off accepted\\n\\nJoin-workspace UI is **mounted and wired** to a join REST seam that MARATHON-7 (open-workspace auto-onboard / join) must implement. Until that endpoint exists, submit shows the server error envelope (or a clear network failure). Create-workspace is the fully working onboarding path today. We accept temporary join failures over inventing a second membership SoT in the SPA task.\\n\\n### Conventions inherited (must not diverge)\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-2**: Product **Huddle**; `GET /` is HTML 200 on every node; `/api/...` JSON; no DinD.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-3**: `UserObj` key set; `{error:{code,message}}`; register/login `{user,token}`; `/api/auth/me`; bearer parsing; username/password validation rules; store token as `huddle.token`.\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-4**: Same `UserObj`; profile PATCH not required in this shell (settings UI is MARATHON-18).\\n\\nFrom **MARATHON-5**: `WorkspaceObj` / `ChannelObj` / full `ReadStateEntry`; `POST/GET /api/workspaces`, `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}`; create body `{slug,name}`; non-member detail → 404.\\n\\n## Interface Contracts\\n\\n### Selector contract (SPA ↔ grader / CUA)\\n\\nAll names below are **`data-testid` values**. They must be present in the DOM when the corresponding UI state is visible (not merely in JS strings). Prefer exactly these strings — no prefixes.\\n\\n| `data-testid` | When visible | Role |\\n|---------------|--------------|------|\\n| `auth-modal` | Unauthenticated (or forced re-auth) | Modal/dialog wrapping the auth form |\\n| `auth-form` | Inside auth modal | `\\u003cform\\u003e` for register or login |\\n| `auth-submit` | Inside auth form | Submit control |\\n| `auth-toggle` | Inside auth modal | Control that switches register ↔ login mode |\\n| `auth-error` | After failed auth attempt | Visible text node showing `error.message` (or client validation message). **Must not** be empty/invisible on 400/401/409. |\\n| `workspace-create-form` | Authenticated empty / onboarding | Form to create workspace (`slug` + `name`) |\\n| `empty-state-create-workspace` | Authenticated with **zero** workspaces | Empty-state control/region that focuses or reveals create form |\\n| `join-workspace-form` | Authenticated empty / onboarding | Form to join by workspace slug |\\n| `join-workspace-slug` | Inside join form | Text input for slug |\\n| `join-workspace-submit` | Inside join form | Submit control |\\n| `join-workspace-error` | After failed join | Visible error text |\\n| `current-user` | Authenticated shell | Shows session user’s `display_name` (fallback `username`) |\\n| `logout-btn` | Authenticated shell | Clears token and returns to auth modal |\\n| `workspace-header` | Authenticated **with** current workspace | Shows workspace identity (`name` and/or `slug`) |\\n| `channel-list` | Authenticated with current workspace | Container for non-DM channels (may be empty of children until channels load / MARATHON-17) |\\n| `dms-list` | Authenticated with current workspace | Container for DM channels (empty until MARATHON-9/17) |\\n\\n**Auth form fields (required for drivability, not all named in the task list):**\\n\\n| `data-testid` | Element |\\n|---------------|---------|\\n| `auth-username` | Username input |\\n| `auth-password` | Password input |\\n| `auth-display-name` | Optional display name; **visible in register mode only** |\\n\\n**Workspace create fields:**\\n\\n| `data-testid` | Element |\\n|---------------|---------|\\n| `workspace-slug` | Slug input |\\n| `workspace-name` | Name input |\\n| `workspace-create-submit` | Submit |\\n| `workspace-create-error` | Visible error |\\n\\n**Shell slots for dependents (mount now, behavior later):**\\n\\n| `data-testid` | Behavior in this task |\\n|---------------|----------------------|\\n| `message-pane` | Always present when shell is shown; may show placeholder copy (“Select a channel” / empty). **No** message composer required here. |\\n| `thread-panel` | Present in DOM; **`hidden` / not displayed** by default (`display:none` or equivalent). MARATHON-17 opens it. |\\n\\n### Token storage contract (browser ↔ SPA)\\n\\n| Operation | Behavior |\\n|-----------|----------|\\n| **Write (register/login success)** | `localStorage.setItem(\\\"huddle.token\\\", token)` where `token` is the opaque string from the API. Also remove stale fallback keys if present (optional hygiene). |\\n| **Read (boot / API client)** | First non-empty string among, in order: `huddle.token`, `huddle_token`, `token`. Treat whitespace-only as missing. |\\n| **Clear (logout or 401 from `/me`)** | Remove **all** of: `huddle.token`, `huddle_token`, `token`. |\\n| **Workspace slug persist** | On successful workspace select/create/restore: `localStorage.setItem(\\\"huddle.workspaceSlug\\\", slug)`. **Do not** clear this on logout (required for “logout/login restores same workspace”). |\\n| **Negative** | Must **not** store the bearer in cookies, `sessionStorage` only, or URL query strings. |\\n\\n### Seam: Browser ↔ `GET /` (and static assets)\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Server (each node)** | `GET /` → **200** `text/html` document that boots the SPA (title/brand includes **Huddle**). Serve `/static/*` assets with correct MIME types. No auth required. |\\n| **Client** | Load JS; run boot sequence below. |\\n\\n**Failure / slow:** TCP errors until node respawn (≤60s) — same as MARATHON-2. Asset 404 → blank UI; implementer must keep relative paths correct.\\n\\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/auth/register`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client** | Body `{username, password, display_name?}` matching MARATHON-3. Disable `auth-submit` while in flight. On **201**: store token, set session user from `user`, close/hide auth modal, continue boot (list workspaces). On **400/409**: show `error.message` in `auth-error` (visible). On network/5xx: show a generic visible error in `auth-error`. |\\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-3). |\\n\\n**Auto-login:** Register success **is** login — do **not** require a second login call. Token from register response is sufficient.\\n\\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/auth/login`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client** | Body `{username, password}`. Same storage + navigation as register. On **401/400**: visible `auth-error` with `error.message`. |\\n| **Server** | Unchanged. |\\n\\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `GET /api/auth/me`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client** | On boot if a token is readable: call with bearer. While pending: show a lightweight boot placeholder; **do not** flash the auth modal if a token exists. On **200**: set session user from `user`. On **401**: clear all token keys; show auth modal. |\\n| **Server** | Unchanged. |\\n\\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `GET /api/workspaces` / `POST /api/workspaces` / `GET /api/workspaces/{slug}`\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client** | All calls send bearer. **List** after auth: if `workspaces.length === 0`, show empty state (`empty-state-create-workspace` + create + join forms). If non-empty: prefer `huddle.workspaceSlug` if it appears in the list; else first list item (sorted as server returns). **Create**: `POST` `{slug,name}`; on **201** persist slug, load detail, enter shell. On **400/409** show `workspace-create-error`. **Detail**: populate `workspace-header`, split `channels` into `channel-list` (`is_dm === false`) and `dms-list` (`is_dm === true`); ignore `read_state` badges in this task (optional no-op). On detail **404**: clear invalid stored slug, fall back to list/empty. On any **401**: logout locally. |\\n| **Server** | Unchanged (MARATHON-5). |\\n\\n**Channel row markup (minimal, for MARATHON-17):** each channel entry **should** expose `data-channel-id=\\\"{id}\\\"` and `data-channel-name=\\\"{name}\\\"` when listed. Display name may show `#` prefix for non-DM; stored `name` remains without `#`.\\n\\n### Seam: SPA ↔ `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join` (client locked here; server owned by MARATHON-7)\\n\\n| Side | Responsibility |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| **Client** | Body `{}` (ignore extras). Bearer required. Disable submit while in flight. On **200** with `{workspace: WorkspaceObj}` (optional `channels` / `read_state` if server returns them): persist slug, enter shell (fetch detail if channels omitted). On **4xx**: show `error.message` in `join-workspace-error`. |\\n| **Server (MARATHON-7)** | For `join_mode=open`, add caller as `member` if not already; return 200. For `invite_only`, **403** (invitations are MARATHON-12). Unknown slug → **404** envelope. Idempotent if already a member → **200**. |\\n\\n**Until MARATHON-7 lands:** SPA still renders join controls; failed submit must surface a visible error (not a silent no-op).\\n\\n### HTTP client rules (SPA owns)\\n\\n1. `Content-Type: application/json` on POST bodies.\\n2. Parse JSON error envelope; never assume FastAPI `detail`.\\n3. Timeouts: recommend ~15s; on abort/network error show visible error on the active form.\\n4. Do not retry 401/409 blindly; do not infinite-retry `/me`.\\n\\n### Auth modal UX\\n\\n- Default mode on first visit: **register** (sign-up), matching “Sign-up form with visible error…”.\\n- `auth-toggle` switches to login and back; update submit label/copy accordingly.\\n- Client-side pre-check may mirror username/password rules for faster UX, but **server messages win** on response.\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n### Browser (no SQLite changes in this task)\\n\\n| Key | Type | Lifetime | Notes |\\n|-----|------|----------|-------|\\n| `localStorage[\\\"huddle.token\\\"]` | string | Until logout / 401 | Canonical bearer |\\n| `localStorage[\\\"huddle_token\\\"]` | string | Read fallback only | Accepted fallback |\\n| `localStorage[\\\"token\\\"]` | string | Read fallback only | Accepted fallback |\\n| `localStorage[\\\"huddle.workspaceSlug\\\"]` | string | Survives logout | Last workspace slug |\\n\\n### In-memory SPA state (not persisted)\\n\\n| Field | Type | Notes |\\n|-------|------|-------|\\n| `user` | `UserObj` \\\\| null | From register/login/`/me` |\\n| `workspaces` | `WorkspaceObj[]` | From list |\\n| `currentWorkspace` | `WorkspaceObj` \\\\| null | Selected |\\n| `channels` | `ChannelObj[]` | From detail |\\n| `authMode` | `\\\"register\\\"` \\\\| `\\\"login\\\"` | Modal mode |\\n| `threadOpen` | boolean | Default `false` |\\n\\n### Server schema\\n\\n**No migration.** This task does not alter SQLite. Backward compatible with migrations v0–v2.\\n\\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\\n\\n### Create\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `static/index.html` | SPA shell markup: auth modal, empty/onboarding, three-pane layout; all required `data-testid`s; `\\u003ctitle\\u003eHuddle\\u003c/title\\u003e`; script `type=\\\"module\\\"` entry. |\\n| `static/css/app.css` | Layout for 1280×900: coloured sidebar (≥~220px), message pane flex-grow, thread panel (~320px) hidden by default; auth modal overlay; visible error styles (not `visibility:hidden` when populated). |\\n| `static/js/storage.js` | Token read/write/clear with fallbacks; workspace slug get/set. |\\n| `static/js/api.js` | `api(method, path, {token, body})` → JSON; maps envelope errors. |\\n| `static/js/auth_ui.js` | Register/login toggle, submit handlers, auto-login on register, error rendering. |\\n| `static/js/shell.js` | Empty state, create/join forms, workspace header, channel/dms lists, logout, hash routing. |\\n| `static/js/app.js` | Boot: read token → `/me` → list → restore slug → render. |\\n\\n(Implementer may collapse JS files if behavior and selectors match; names above are the preferred split.)\\n\\n### Modify\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `server/app.py` | Replace inline stub HTML with `FileResponse` to `static/index.html` (path resolved from app root). Mount `StaticFiles` at `/static` pointing at `static/`. Keep `/api/health` and routers unchanged. Ensure `/` is registered **before** any catch-all; do not shadow `/api/*`. |\\n| `tests/test_health.py` | Keep asserting `GET /` 200 HTML + `\\\"Huddle\\\"` in body (still true). Optionally assert a stable selector string appears in HTML (e.g. `data-testid=\\\"auth-form\\\"`) — recommended, not mandatory if covered by a new SPA test file. |\\n| `tests/test_spa_shell.py` (create) | TestClient: `/` contains required testids; `/static/...` 200; optional auth flow via API + HTML presence (no browser required for unit). |\\n\\n### Do not modify\\n\\n| File | Reason |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `server/auth/*`, `server/workspaces/*`, `server/users/*` | Contracts already shipped; SPA is consumer only |\\n| `start.sh` | No build step to add |\\n| `timer.sh` | Harness-owned |\\n\\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\\n\\n### Build order within this task\\n\\n1. Static files + `app.py` serve path (unblocks `GET /` HTML checks).\\n2. `storage.js` + `api.js`.\\n3. Auth modal + register/login/`/me` boot.\\n4. Workspace list/create/empty state + slug restore.\\n5. Shell chrome (sidebar colour, header, channel/dms lists, logout, thread slot).\\n6. Join form wired to join seam (tolerate backend absence via visible error).\\n\\n### Parallelism\\n\\n- Can implement entirely in parallel with MARATHON-6/8/9/10/… **except** join success depends on MARATHON-7’s open-workspace join/auto-onboard.\\n- MARATHON-17/18 **must** land after this shell (they depend on this task).\\n\\n### Seams this task owns for dependents\\n\\n| Contract | Consumer |\\n|----------|----------|\\n| `data-testid` shell + auth set above | QA / CUA; MARATHON-17/18 |\\n| `huddle.token` + fallbacks + `huddle.workspaceSlug` | All later SPA tasks |\\n| Hash route `#/w/{slug}` + in-memory workspace/channel selection hooks | MARATHON-17 |\\n| Hidden `thread-panel` slot | MARATHON-17 |\\n| `channel-list` / `dms-list` containers + `data-channel-id` | MARATHON-17 |\\n| Client call shape `POST /api/workspaces/{slug}/join` | MARATHON-7 must implement server |\\n\\n### Split follow-ups (already exist — do not recreate)\\n\\n- **MARATHON-17** — messages, threads, reactions, channel create/switch UI inside this shell.\\n- **MARATHON-18** — workspace/channel settings modals.\\n- **MARATHON-7** — server join / open auto-onboard so join form succeeds.\\n\\n## Out of Scope (Needs a Separate Task)\\n\\n| Item | Where found | Why excluded |\\n|------|-------------|--------------|\\n| Message composer, edit/delete, reactions, emoji picker | MARATHON-17 description; no message routes yet (MARATHON-8 open) | Dependent SPA task |\\n| Opening/populating `thread-panel` with replies | MARATHON-17 | Shell only mounts hidden slot |\\n| Workspace settings / invitations UI (`workspace-settings-modal`, invitation testids) | MARATHON-18; APIs MARATHON-6/12 | Different task |\\n| Channel create/join/leave/archive/pins REST | `server/channels/store.py` helpers only; no routes | MARATHON-7 |\\n| DM get-or-create | No DM API | MARATHON-9; `dms-list` stays empty-capable |\\n| Profile PATCH UI | `PATCH /api/users/me` exists | MARATHON-18 / settings |\\n| WebSocket subscribe/resume | No WS routes | MARATHON-13 |\\n| Logout token revoke API | MARATHON-3 explicitly out of scope | Client clears storage only |\\n| IRC / Redis fan-out UI | Cluster tasks | Unrelated |\\n| Stub text “Cluster node stub.” | `server/app.py` | Replaced by SPA in this task (in scope to remove) |\\n\\nNeighborhood scan accounted for: `HTMLResponse` stub in `server/app.py`; `tests/test_health.py` + `tests/test_cluster_boot.py` `GET /` HTML assertions (remain valid if brand “Huddle” + HTML document preserved); no existing `static/` tree; no `localStorage` / `data-testid` hits in-repo yet.\\n\\n## Edge Cases \\u0026 Error Handling\\n\\n| Case | Expected behavior |\\n|------|-------------------|\\n| Invalid register username/password (client or 400) | Show message in **visible** `auth-error`; stay on form; do **not** store token |\\n| Register username taken (409) | Visible `auth-error` with server message; no token write |\\n| Login bad credentials (401) | Visible `auth-error`; no token write |\\n| Register success | Store token; treat as logged in; **no** manual login step |\\n| Boot with valid token | `/me` then workspace flow; auth modal **not** shown |\\n| Boot with garbage token | `/me` 401 → clear tokens → auth modal |\\n| Boot with fallback key only (`token` set, `huddle.token` absent) | Read fallback; on next successful login/register rewrite canonical `huddle.token` |\\n| Logout | Clear token keys; show auth modal; **keep** `huddle.workspaceSlug`; clear in-memory user/channels |\\n| Login after logout with same user | Restore workspace from `huddle.workspaceSlug` if still a member; else first workspace or empty state |\\n| Stored slug for workspace user left / never joined | Detail 404 → drop slug selection; re-list; do not loop |\\n| Create workspace validation/conflict | Visible `workspace-create-error`; remain on form |\\n| Join before MARATHON-7 (404/405/network) | Visible `join-workspace-error`; do not fake membership client-side |\\n| API slow | Disable active submit; keep prior UI; no double-submit |\\n| `GET /` on :8001/:8002 | Same SPA bytes/behavior as :8000 |\\n| Thread panel default | Not visible; must **not** cover message pane at 1280×900 |\\n| Empty channel/dms lists | Containers still present with testids; empty children OK |\\n| Password in DOM errors | Never echo password into `auth-error` |\\n| Unknown JSON fields from server | Ignore extras; do not crash |\\n| `include_archived` | Shell detail calls **omit** query (default hide archived) |\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `GET http://127.0.0.1:800{0,1,2}/` → **200** HTML containing brand **Huddle** and bootstraps the SPA (script/CSS load without 404).\\n2. Unauthenticated visit shows `auth-modal`, `auth-form`, `auth-submit`, `auth-toggle`.\\n3. Sign-up with invalid input (e.g. short password) shows a **visible** error (readable in `auth-error` / form error UI); must **not** set `huddle.token`.\\n4. Sign-up with valid input → **201** path: token stored at `localStorage[\\\"huddle.token\\\"]` (len ≥ 16); user is logged in **without** a separate login submit; auth modal dismissed.\\n5. `auth-toggle` switches to login; successful login also stores `huddle.token` and enters authenticated UI.\\n6. Authenticated zero-workspace state exposes `empty-state-create-workspace`, `workspace-create-form`, and `join-workspace-form` / `join-workspace-slug` / `join-workspace-submit`.\\n7. Creating a workspace via the form calls `POST /api/workspaces` and then shows shell with `workspace-header`, `channel-list`, `dms-list`, `current-user`, `logout-btn`, `message-pane`, and hidden `thread-panel`.\\n8. Sidebar is visually distinct (coloured) from the message pane; workspace identity appears in the sidebar/`workspace-header`.\\n9. Logout via `logout-btn` clears bearer storage (all token keys) and returns to auth UI; `huddle.workspaceSlug` remains.\\n10. Logging in again as the same user restores the previous workspace (same slug in header/lists) without manually re-picking, when membership still exists.\\n11. Layout is usable at **1280×900** without requiring horizontal scrolling for the three-pane shell (thread collapsed).\\n12. Negative: authenticated API calls must **not** omit the `Authorization` header when a token is present.\\n13. Negative: must **not** leave the MARATHON-2 stub-only body (“Cluster node stub”) as the sole `GET /` content.\\n14. Negative: must **not** require Node/npm to build assets for `start.sh` boot.\\n15. Reading a bearer from fallback key `token` or `huddle_token` still authenticates on boot if `/me` succeeds.\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Automated\\n\\n- Extend/keep `tests/test_health.py` + cluster boot: `GET /` HTML 200 + Huddle.\\n- Add `tests/test_spa_shell.py` (TestClient): document contains critical `data-testid`s; `/static/js/app.js` (or chosen entry) returns 200; optional flow register via API then assert token key documented (storage is browser-only — HTML/API integration is enough at unit layer).\\n\\n### Manual / CUA (primary)\\n\\n1. `./start.sh`; open `http://127.0.0.1:8000/` at 1280×900.\\n2. Register invalid user → see error; register valid → land in empty/create state; confirm DevTools `localStorage[\\\"huddle.token\\\"]`.\\n3. Create workspace → sidebar shows name/slug; `#general` appears under `channel-list`.\\n4. Logout → login → same workspace restored.\\n5. Repeat load on `:8001` with same token (paste or shared storage isn’t cross-port — instead register on 8000, copy token into 8001 `localStorage`, reload) → `/me` works (cluster SoT).\\n6. Confirm thread panel not visible; message pane placeholder visible.\\n7. Toggle auth register/login; confirm selectors exist for Playwright (`document.querySelector('[data-testid=\\\"auth-form\\\"]')` etc.).\\n\\n### Out of test scope here\\n\\nFull message/thread/reaction flows (MARATHON-17); settings/invitations (MARATHON-18); successful open-workspace join (blocked on MARATHON-7 server).\",\n  \"design_format\": \"markdown\",\n  \"has_design\": true,\n  \"notes\": \"IMPL: Zero-build SPA at GET / (static/). Token write huddle.token; read fallbacks huddle_token/token. Workspace restore via huddle.workspaceSlug across logout. Join form POSTs /api/workspaces/{slug}/join (server still MARATHON-7). Verified via pytest + Playwright at 1280x900 (register/login/create/logout/restore; thread panel hidden).\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:47.179119571Z\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-08-22T23:35:12.247305911Z\",\n  \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\",\n  \"description\": \"Serve SPA from GET / on any node. Sign-up form with visible error on invalid input; auto-login on success. Logout/login restores same workspace. Store bearer in localStorage huddle.token (or accepted fallbacks). Three-pane layout shell: coloured sidebar + message pane + on-demand thread panel. Workspace identity in sidebar. Stable selectors: auth-form, auth-submit, auth-toggle, auth-modal, workspace-create-form, empty-state-create-workspace, join-workspace-*, current-user, logout-btn, workspace-header, channel-list, dms-list. Drivable at 1280x900.\",\n  \"dependents\": [\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-17\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-16\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"SPA: channels, messages, threads, reactions\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"priority\": 1,\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:56.201269638Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-18\",\n      \"depends_on_id\": \"MARATHON-16\",\n      \"type\": \"blocks\",\n      \"title\": \"SPA: workspace and channel settings UI\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"priority\": 2,\n      \"issue_type\": \"task\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T22:17:56.275071493Z\",\n      \"created_by\": \"marathon-harness\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": 26,\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-16\",\n      \"author\": \"marathon-harness\",\n      \"text\": \"DESIGN-AUTO-APPROVED pass=11\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-08-22T23:29:16.865171828Z\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": 27,\n      \"issue_id\": \"MARATHON-16\",\n      \"author\": \"fron